comments.body:
@jhome2533 
> What should I take a look at?

The bubledevteam should take a look. That's why I addressed them using `@bubbledevteam`. The problem is related to the bubble collector developed by them. They know it best how to fix it.

@jhome2533 First, please do not include the message history if you answer by email. That messes up this issue.
Better comment on GitHub, directly.

Regarding to the logs: either paste a screenshot here or dump table UserErrors from an exported database.

@tolot27 If we (xDrip support) cannot fix this, why do we have it tagged as an xDrip bug?  Isn't that contradictory in terms?

Can we either remove the bug label from this issue, or drop the capability from xDrip completely until the external developers fix it?
Otherwise, if we keep this tagged as an xDrip bug, how is it going to correctly highlight to our xDrip developers what they need to focus on?
